  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "Let r_k(n) count representations of n as an ordered sum of k squares. Jacobi r_2, r_6, r_8 are modified divisor sums; the claim is explicit native_decide-free closed forms on prime powers, e.g. for odd prime p and m>=0, r_8(p^m) = 16 sigma_3(p^m) = 16 (p^{3(m+1)}-1)/(p^3-1), with analogous geometric-series closed forms for r_2(p^m) (divisors mod 4) and r_6(p^m) (twisted divisor sum), via divisors_prime_pow and a parity/character argument.",
    "plain": "AVAILABLE — Do the sibling sum-of-squares counts admit analogous native_decide-free closed forms on prime powers? Jacobi's r₂, r₆, r₈ and Liouville-style formulas are also expressed through (modified) divisor sums; the same divisors_prime_pow + parity strategy may yield symbolic prime-power values for those fam.",
